{"id": "EUVD-2026-38414", "enisaUuid": "7222b884-f4d3-3a12-a980-2c3130ca34f8", "description": "A flaw was found in OpenSSH. This vulnerability, a heap out-of-bounds read, occurs during the cleanup of GSSAPI (Generic Security Service Application Programming Interface) indicators when a trailing NULL termination is missing in the auth-indicators array. A remote attacker, under specific configurations involving GSSAPI authentication and a Kerberos environment, could exploit this to cause the SSH authentication path to crash or abort. This leads to a denial of service (DoS), impacting the availability of the SSH service.", "datePublished": "2026-06-23T03:37:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T22:41:04", "baseScore": 3.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:36759", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47756", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:47757", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:54387", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:58981", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-55654", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2462493"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5mx2-7g4j-9m39", "CVE-2026-55654"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.65, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1800b608-29f4-31cd-bc54-d80cd08c0046", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787135742"}, {"id": "30194496-fdc8-3702-9f09-70676179c67c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:9.9p1-25.el10_2"}, {"id": "76975f68-5e1f-3da0-86e4-d2f7a1e7166b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786435483"}, {"id": "800b2138-2dff-36ca-8427-d440fa927db9", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patc